Tension: guard BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD on OGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE
==========================================================================

Why this patch exists
---------------------
OGRE-Next's OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt:403 unconditionally seeds

    set( BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD "src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp" )

and CMake/Utils/OgreAddTargets.cmake:54 then does

    set(_SOURCES ${_PRIMARY} ${_EXCLUDES})

where `_EXCLUDES` contains the `SEPARATE` list passed to `ogre_add_library`.
That list is *appended* to the target's sources, not subtracted from them. The
`if (OGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE)` block at OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt:354 only
adds the header, source and FreeImage_LIBRARIES when the option is ON; it never
removes anything when it is OFF.

Because of line 403, `-DOGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE=OFF` leaves
`src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp` in `_EXCLUDES`, forcing `ogre_add_library` to
compile it even when FreeImage is disabled. The translation unit includes
`<FreeImage.h>`, so building without FreeImage installed fails:

    OgreMain/src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp:48:10: fatal error:
      FreeImage.h: No such file or directory

(or at link time on a machine where FreeImage happens to be installed).

This patch fixes the root cause in CMake by guarding the initialization of
`BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD` with `if (OGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE)`.
When FreeImage is disabled, the file is never added to `BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD`,
so it is never added to `_SOURCES` and never compiled. When FreeImage is enabled,
it remains in the SEPARATE list for unity builds as intended.

Upstream state
--------------
Unfixed as of ogre-next master (pinned here at 475f783d76). If upstream adds
the guard in CMake, this patch becomes a no-op (patch -N --forward reports
"previously applied" and skips); if upstream changes the surrounding lines,
bootstrap.mjs fails loudly with the rejected hunk rather than silently skipping.

Source
------
Measured in this repo's FreeImage-removal experiment against the pinned submodule:
OgreNextMain and the full tree build without FreeImage, and `ldd` lists no
libfreeimage.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.mjs before CMake configuration. It is never edited
in place by hand: AGENTS.md rule 1 keeps third_party/ogre-next read-only, and
the build reproduces through `npm run bootstrap`.

--- a/OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -400,7 +400,10 @@
 
 set (TARGET_LINK_FLAGS "")
 
-set( BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD "src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp" )
+set( BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD "" )
+if (OGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE)
+	list( APPEND BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD "src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp" )
+endif ()
 
 # setup OgreMain target
 if (WINDOWS_STORE OR WINDOWS_PHONE)
